This file describes how to build Airoha ATF from sources.

REQUIREMENTS:
 * Airoha AN7581/AN7583 SDK (2025Q1 or newer)
 * Airoha EN7523 SDK (for en7523 builds only)

1) Build Airoha SDK. The following utility is required

    * trx-airoha -- airoha specific trx utility

2) In the EN7523 SoC case

   * Create 'plat/ecnt/blobs/en7523' directory

   * Fill 'plat/ecnt/blobs/en7523' directory with the files from
     Airoha EN7523 SDK. The following file structure MUST be created:

        /"
        +-- bl1.bin"
        +-- bl22"
        |     +-- dramc.o"
        |     +-- dramc_pi_basic_api.o"
        |     +-- dramc_pi_calibration_api.o"
        |     +-- dramc_pi_main.o"
        |     +-- efuse_load.o"
        |     +-- efuse.o"
        |     +-- hal_io.o"
        +-- bl23"
        |     +-- cortex_a53.o"
        |     +-- ecnt_npu_img.o"
        |     +-- efuse_load.o"
        |     +-- efuse.o"
        +-- bl31.bin"

     bl1.bin, bl31.bin     -- take files from directory
                              ${SDK32}/airoha_feeds/package/airoha/bootloader/bootloader/unopen_img/${profile}/atf

     dramc.o, cortex_a53.o -- take files from directory
                              ${SDK32}/airoha_feeds/package/airoha/bootloader/bootloader/unopen_img/${profile}/atf/bl2

     other object files    -- extract from archieve
                              ${SDK32}/airoha_feeds/package/airoha/bootloader/bootloader/unopen_img/${profile}/atf/bl2/libbl2.a

   Notes on bl23/:
     * ecnt_npu_img.o is required: make_helpers/build_macros.mk copies it
       unconditionally (the recipe has no leading '-', so the build fails
       if it is missing).  It only carries the NPU firmware
       (npu_rv32.bin / npu_data.bin) inside the BL23 image.
     * cortex_a53.o is listed above for parity with the vendor layout, but
       this tree does not copy it: BL2/BL23 build lib/cpus/aarch64/cortex_a53.S
       from source instead.  Installing it is harmless.

2a) Extracting the blobs from a vendor ATF release (no SDK required)

   If you already have the ATF artefacts of a working vendor firmware
   (in this repository they are kept under reference/, see
   reference/UNION_EN7523_GLIBC_7916_7916_ActiveEthWan_demo/atf), the blobs
   can be produced with:

     REF=reference/UNION_EN7523_GLIBC_7916_7916_ActiveEthWan_demo/atf
     BLOB=plat/ecnt/blobs/en7523
     AR=$(command -v arm-none-eabi-ar || echo ar)

     mkdir -p ${BLOB}/bl22 ${BLOB}/bl23

     # BL1/BL31 are plain binaries shipped next to the ATF tree
     cp ${REF}/bl1.bin ${REF}/bl31.bin ${BLOB}/

     # dramc.o is a loose object file (it is not part of libbl2.a)
     cp ${REF}/bl2/dramc.o ${BLOB}/bl22/

     # everything else lives inside the libbl2.a archive
     ar -x ${REF}/bl2/libbl2.a \
        efuse.o efuse_load.o hal_io.o \
        dramc_pi_basic_api.o dramc_pi_calibration_api.o dramc_pi_main.o \
        ecnt_npu_img.o
     mv efuse.o efuse_load.o hal_io.o \
        dramc_pi_basic_api.o dramc_pi_calibration_api.o dramc_pi_main.o \
        ${BLOB}/bl22/
     mv efuse.o efuse_load.o ecnt_npu_img.o ${BLOB}/bl23/

   Do NOT mix objects coming from different vendor releases: the DRAMC
   objects of a build that boots with wrong DRAM contents are NOT
   interchangeable with a good one, and mixing them silently produces a
   broken image (wrong DRAM size, corrupted memory).  Verify the result by
   the DRAMC banner, e.g. "EN7523DRAMC V0.2" followed by
   "DRAM size=512MB".

3) Prepare building directory with the following command

     ${this_repo_path}/scripts/build-prepare.sh

4) Enter to the build directory

     cd atf-airoha-build/build

5) If necessary, edit build-${SOC}.sh scripts to tune your build options

   You may need to tune following options

     * OPTEE                               -- enable optee
     * OVERRIDE_UBI_START_ADDR             -- where to find UBI spi-nand partition
     * TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT           -- search for fip image in GPT 'fip' partition
     * OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET  -- read fip image from specified eMMC offset
                                              if TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT is not set
                                              or GPT 'fip' partition was not found

   Current settings are:
     * OPTEE=no
     * OVERRIDE_UBI_START_ADDR=0x100000
     * TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT -- enabled
     * OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET=0x84000

   OpenWrt compatible settings are:
     * optee -- disabled
     * OVERRIDE_UBI_START_ADDR=0x20000
     * TCSUPPORT_GPT_ATF_SUPPORT is not set
     * OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET is not set or OVERRIDE_PLAT_ECNT_BL31_FIP_OFFSET=0x20000

   Please fix in the script all places where these defines are mentioned.

   WARNING: OpenWRT settings are incompatible with spi-nand flashes that
            have 256 KB erase block.

6) Build ATF images

      $ ./build-${SOC}.sh

   resulting images will be stored in

     out/${SOC}/

   directory

   Alternatively, the in-tree entry point 'build.sh' at the root of this
   repository performs the same steps without the 'build-prepare.sh'
   out-of-tree setup.  It needs the cross toolchain in the PATH:

      $ SOC=en7523 ./build.sh bl2      # BL21 + BL22(lzma) + BL23(lzma)
      $ SOC=en7523 ./build.sh bl31     # pack the prebuilt BL1/BL31 blobs
      $ SOC=en7523 ./build.sh all

   Artefacts are written to 'output/en7523/':

      en7523-bl2.bin    combined BL2 (bl21.bin + bl22.lzma + bl23.lzma
                        + flash table)
      bl21.bin          stage 1, not compressed
      bl22.lzma         stage 2, carries the DRAM calibration
      bl23.lzma         stage 3, full featured
      en7523-bl1.bin    prebuilt blob, copied from blobs/en7523/bl1.bin
      bl31.bin          prebuilt blob, copied from blobs/en7523/bl31.bin
      bl31.lzma         prebuilt blob, copied from blobs/en7523/bl31.lzma

   Sanity checks: the decompressed BL22/BL23 images must stay below the
   0x19000 byte BL2 staging buffer.

7) You may also run 'build-flash-images.sh' to create ready to flash ATF images

8) Have fun!
